.TH CHTTPCLIENT_ASYNC_RESULT_FREE 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttpclient_async_result_free \- free a chttpcli_async_result_t
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/chttpclient.h>

void chttpclient_async_result_free(chttpcli_async_result_t *result);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
This function frees a chttpcli_async_result_t that
chttpclient_async_result_get returned. It does NOT free result->resp,
so when result->rv == ccol_success you have to free that first, with
its own call to chttpclient_resp_free. It does NOT free the future
either: pair it with exactly one separate ctpool_future_free call,
before or after this one (the order does not matter). The result keeps
its own copy of the client's allocator, so this call is valid before
or after chttpclient_destroy of that client.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
result The result to free. NULL is a safe no-op.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
None.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttpclient_async_result_get (3),
.BR chttpclient_resp_free (3),
.BR ctpool_future_free (3)
